<?xml version="1.0" encoding="ISO-8859-1"?>
<wps:ProcessDescriptions xmlns:wps="http://www.opengis.net/wps/1.0.0" xmlns:ows="http://www.opengis.net/ows/1.1" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.opengis.net/wps/1.0.0 schemas/wps/1.0.0/wpsDescribeProcess_response.xsd" service="WPS" version="1.0.0" xml:lang="en-US">
	<ProcessDescription wps:processVersion="1" storeSupported="true" statusSupported="false">
		<ows:Identifier>MiraMon:DXFVEC:Param1:0</ows:Identifier>
		<ows:Title>DXFVEC 0</ows:Title>
		<ows:Abstract>CONTENTS INFORMATION:Shows a DXF contents enumeration. It presents the number of polylines, lines, arcs, circles, ellipses, solids, points, texts and blocks splitted by layers. Inside block context, for each layer it appears the name and the number of blocks with this name.</ows:Abstract>
<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Title:Conversion between DXF files and VEC files." />
<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Abstract:This program performs the conversion between DXF files (obtained with DXFOUT of AutoCAD, export of CorelDraw, etc.) and vectorial files, either topological structured (grouped in a MMM file) or not (VEC format)."/>
		<DataInputs>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Opcio</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Option</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>0. Information on file contents</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param1" />
					<LiteralData>
						<ows:AllowedValues>
							<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer "> integer</ows:DataType>
							<ows:Value>0</ows:Value>
						</ows:AllowedValues>
					</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Fitx1</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>File 1</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>DXF File</ows:Abstract>
						<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2" />
					<ComplexData>
						<Default>
							<Format>
								<MimeType>application/x-dfx</MimeType>
								<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
							</Format>
						</Default>
						<Supported>
							<Format>
								<MimeType>application/x-dfx</MimeType>
								<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
							</Format>
						</Supported>
					</ComplexData>
			</Input>
	</DataInputs>
		<ProcessOutputs>
			<Output>
				<ows:Identifier>FitxText</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Text File</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the name of a text file that will keep a copy of the information shown in the screen. It can be used only with option 0.
				</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param3" />
						<ComplexOutput>
							<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-txt</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-txt</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
						</ComplexOutput>
			</Output>
		</ProcessOutputs>
	</ProcessDescription>
	<ProcessDescription wps:processVersion="1" storeSupported="true" statusSupported="false">
		<ows:Identifier>MiraMon:DXFVEC:Param1:1</ows:Identifier>
		<ows:Title>DXFVEC 1</ows:Title>
		<ows:Abstract>DXF LINES, POLYLINES, ARCS, CIRCLES, ELLIPSES AND SOLIDS WILL BE TRANSFORMED TO VEC LINES OR POLYGONS.
If the program detects that all the polylines are closed, either in the DXF file definition or by detecting that the extreme coordinates are equal, it will document the objects as being of type "polygon"; in the opposite case it will document them as of type "line".
Layer that contains the entity becomes attribute in VEC file.
The number of vertex in a polyline is almost unlimited.
The program takes parameter tolerance from command line to convert arcs, circles and ellipses to polylines. Tolerance is the maximum permitted error when translating DXF lines and circles to VEC polylines. (maximum distance between arc and chord). The last versions of DXF format (AcadCAD 2000) allows you to define curvatures between the vertices of a polyline object. The tolerance also applies in these objects. If a 0 is indicated, the number of vertex is limited to one for degree. Tolerance is only used in option 1.</ows:Abstract>
		<DataInputs>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Opcio</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Option</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>1. Lines, polylines, arcs, circles, ellipses and solids -> lines or polygons, depending on whether they are opened or not</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param1" />
					<LiteralData>
						<ows:AllowedValues>
							<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer "> integer</ows:DataType>
							<ows:Value>1</ows:Value>
						</ows:AllowedValues>
					</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>F_DXF</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>DXF File</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Name of the DXF file to convert</ows:Abstract>
						<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2" />
					<ComplexData>
						<Default>
							<Format>
								<MimeType>application/x-dfx</MimeType>
								<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
							</Format>
						</Default>
						<Supported>
							<Format>
								<MimeType>application/x-dfx</MimeType>
								<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
							</Format>
						</Supported>
					</ComplexData>
			</Input>	
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>TipusAtribut</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Type of Attribute</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract><![CDATA[<ul><li>1 Integer numbres ignoring texts and rounding if necessary.</li><li>2 Real numbers ignoring texts.</li><li> 3 3 Alphanumerical (texts and numbers) (not valid with altimetry entities filters).</li></ul>]]></ows:Abstract>
						<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param4" />
						<LiteralData>
						<ows:AllowedValues>
							<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer "> integer</ows:DataType>
							<ows:Value>1</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>2</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>3</ows:Value>
						</ows:AllowedValues>
					</LiteralData>
			</Input>			
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Filtre</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Filter</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Objects filter:<![CDATA[<ul><li>
    1 Objects from all the layers</li><li>2 Objects from one layer</li><li>3 Objects from several layers from a file with one column equivalencies.</li><li>4 One text in any layer (only valid in options 3, 4 and 5).</li><li>5 Several texts in all the layers from a file of equivalences. (only valid in options 3, 4 and 5).</li><li>6 Altimetry: attribute will be deduced from the Z of the first vertex.</li><li>7 Altimetry from a file that contains the desired layers.</li><li>8 Block descripcions</li></ul>]]></ows:Abstract>
						<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param5" />
						<LiteralData>
						<ows:AllowedValues>
							<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer "> integer</ows:DataType>
							<ows:Value>1</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>2</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>3</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>4</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>5</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>6</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>7</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>8</ows:Value>
						</ows:AllowedValues>
					</LiteralData>
			</Input>			
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>N_Decimals</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Number of Decimals</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the number of decimal figures written in the coordinates of the output file; its default value is 6.</ows:Abstract>
						<LiteralData>
						<ows:AllowedValues>
							<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer "> integer</ows:DataType>
							<ows:Value>1</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>2</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>3</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>4</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>5</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>6</ows:Value>
						</ows:AllowedValues>
						<DefaultValue>6</DefaultValue>
					</LiteralData>
			</Input>	
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Tolerància</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Tolerance</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the maximum tolerated error when converting arcs, circles ellipses and curvatures between vertices DXF to VEC polylines. It can be used only with option 1. By default is 0.</ows:Abstract>
						<LiteralData>
						<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#decimal">decimal</ows:DataType>
							<ows:AnyValue/>
						</ows:AllowedValues>
						<DefaultValue>0</DefaultValue>
					</LiteralData>
			</Input>			
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>3D</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>3D</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>1 means you want to importar 3rt dimension from DXF file. 0 means you don't want to import. If the parameter isn't indicated, the program determines if DXF file si 2D o 3D file and choose the appropriated VEC format.</ows:Abstract>
						<LiteralData>
						<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer "> integer</ows:DataType>
							<ows:Value>0</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>1</ows:Value>	
						</ows:AllowedValues>
						<DefaultValue>0</DefaultValue>
					</LiteralData>
			</Input>			
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FITX_EQUIV</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Equivalences file</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the name of the equivalences file when using entities filters 3, 5 and 7. If it isn't indicated, the name will be asked during execution.</ows:Abstract>
						<ComplexData>
						<Default>
							<Format>
								<MimeType>application/x-txt</MimeType>
								<Encoding>text</Encoding>
							</Format>
						</Default>
						<Supported>
							<Format>
								<MimeType>application/x-txt</MimeType>
								<Encoding>text</Encoding>
							</Format>
						</Supported>
					</ComplexData>
			</Input>	
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>CAPA</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Capa</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the name of the layer to import using the filter 2. If it isn't indicated, the name will be asked during execution.</ows:Abstract>
						<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#text">text</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>ATRIBUT</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Attribute</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the attribute that substitutes the name of the layer to import using the filters 2 and 3. If it isn't indicated and you have indicated /CAPA, it takes the same value; on the contrary, it will be asked during execution.</ows:Abstract>
						<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#text">text</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>			
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>TEXT</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Text</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the name of the text to import. If it isn't indicated, the name will be asked during execution.</ows:Abstract>
						<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#text">text</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>	
			</DataInputs>
		<ProcessOutputs>
			<Output>
				<ows:Identifier>F_VEC</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Vectorial file</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Usually it is the name of the output VEC file. It is the extraction directory when using the filter 8.
				</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param3" />
						<ComplexOutput>
							<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-VEC</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-VEC</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
						</ComplexOutput>
			</Output>
		</ProcessOutputs>
	</ProcessDescription>
	<ProcessDescription wps:processVersion="1" storeSupported="true" statusSupported="false">
		<ows:Identifier>MiraMon:DXFVEC:Param1:2</ows:Identifier>
		<ows:Title>DXFVEC 2</ows:Title>
		<ows:Abstract>DXF POINTS WILL BE TRANSFORMED TO VEC POINTS.
The name of the layer that contains the entity becomes point attribute in VEC file.</ows:Abstract>
		<DataInputs>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Opcio</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Option</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>2. Points -> points</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param1" />
					<LiteralData>
						<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer "> integer</ows:DataType>
							<ows:Value>2</ows:Value>
						</ows:AllowedValues>
					</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>F_DXF</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>DXF File</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Name of the DXF file to convert</ows:Abstract>
						<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2" />
					<ComplexData>
						<Default>
							<Format>
								<MimeType>application/x-dfx</MimeType>
								<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
							</Format>
						</Default>
						<Supported>
							<Format>
								<MimeType>application/x-dfx</MimeType>
								<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
							</Format>
						</Supported>
					</ComplexData>
			</Input>	
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>TipusAtribut</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Type of Attribute</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract><![CDATA[<ul><li>1 Integer numbres ignoring texts and rounding if necessary.</li><li>2 Real numbers ignoring texts.</li><li> 3 3 Alphanumerical (texts and numbers) (not valid with altimetry entities filters).</li></ul>]]></ows:Abstract>
						<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param4" />
						<LiteralData>
						<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer "> integer</ows:DataType>
							<ows:Value>1</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>2</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>3</ows:Value>
						</ows:AllowedValues>
					</LiteralData>
			</Input>			
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Filtre</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Filter</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Objects filter:<![CDATA[<ul><li>
    1 Objects from all the layers</li><li>2 Objects from one layer</li><li>3 Objects from several layers from a file with one column equivalencies.</li><li>4 One text in any layer (only valid in options 3, 4 and 5).</li><li>5 Several texts in all the layers from a file of equivalences. (only valid in options 3, 4 and 5).</li><li>6 Altimetry: attribute will be deduced from the Z of the first vertex.</li><li>7 Altimetry from a file that contains the desired layers.</li><li>8 Block descripcions</li></ul>]]></ows:Abstract>
						<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param5" />
						<LiteralData>
						<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer "> integer</ows:DataType>
							<ows:Value>1</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>2</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>3</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>4</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>5</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>6</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>7</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>8</ows:Value>
						</ows:AllowedValues>
					</LiteralData>
			</Input>			
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>N_Decimals</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Number of Decimals</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the number of decimal figures written in the coordinates of the output file; its default value is 6.</ows:Abstract>
						<LiteralData>
						<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer "> integer</ows:DataType>
							<ows:Value>1</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>2</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>3</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>4</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>5</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>6</ows:Value>
						</ows:AllowedValues>
						<DefaultValue>6</DefaultValue>
					</LiteralData>
			</Input>	
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Tolerància</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Tolerance</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the maximum tolerated error when converting arcs, circles ellipses and curvatures between vertices DXF to VEC polylines. It can be used only with option 1. By default is 0.</ows:Abstract>
						<LiteralData>
						<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer "> integer</ows:DataType>
							<ows:AnyValue/>
						</ows:AllowedValues>
						<DefaultValue>0</DefaultValue>
					</LiteralData>
			</Input>			
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>3D</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>3D</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>1 means you want to import 3rt dimension from DXF file. 0 means you don't want to import. If the parameter isn't indicated, the program determines if DXF file if 2D o 3D file and choose the appropriated VEC format.</ows:Abstract>
						<LiteralData>
						<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer "> integer</ows:DataType>
							<ows:Value>0</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>1</ows:Value>	
						</ows:AllowedValues>
						<DefaultValue>0</DefaultValue>
					</LiteralData>
			</Input>			
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FITX_EQUIV</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Equivalences file</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the name of the equivalences file when using entities filters 3, 5 and 7. If it isn't indicated, the name will be asked during execution.</ows:Abstract>
						<ComplexData>
						<Default>
							<Format>
								<MimeType>application/x-txt</MimeType>
								<Encoding>text</Encoding>
							</Format>
						</Default>
						<Supported>
							<Format>
								<MimeType>application/x-txt</MimeType>
								<Encoding>text</Encoding>
							</Format>
						</Supported>
					</ComplexData>
			</Input>	
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>CAPA</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Capa</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the name of the layer to import using the filter 2. If it isn't indicated, the name will be asked during execution.</ows:Abstract>
						<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#text">text</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>ATRIBUT</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Attribute</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the attribute that substitutes the name of the layer to import using the filters 2 and 3. If it isn't indicated and you have indicated /CAPA, it takes the same value; on the contrary, it will be asked during execution.</ows:Abstract>
						<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#text">text</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>			
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>TEXT</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Text</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the name of the text to import. If it isn't indicated, the name will be asked during execution.</ows:Abstract>
						<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#text">text</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>	
			</DataInputs>
		<ProcessOutputs>
			<Output>
				<ows:Identifier>F_VEC</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Vectorial file</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Usually it is the name of the output VEC file. It is the extraction directory when using the filter 8.
				</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param3" />
						<ComplexOutput>
							<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-VEC</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-VEC</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
						</ComplexOutput>
			</Output>
		</ProcessOutputs>
	</ProcessDescription>
	<ProcessDescription wps:processVersion="1" storeSupported="true" statusSupported="false">
		<ows:Identifier>MiraMon:DXFVEC:Param1:3</ows:Identifier>
		<ows:Title>DXFVEC 3</ows:Title>
		<ows:Abstract>DXF TEXTS WILL BE TRANSFORMED TO VEC POINTS.
Entity text becomes point attribute in VEC file.</ows:Abstract>
		<DataInputs>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Opcio</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Option</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>3. Texts -> points with text value as attribute</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param1" />
					<LiteralData>
						<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer "> integer</ows:DataType>
							<ows:Value>3</ows:Value>
						</ows:AllowedValues>
					</LiteralData>
			</Input>
	<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>F_DXF</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>DXF File</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Name of the DXF file to convert</ows:Abstract>
						<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2" />
					<ComplexData>
						<Default>
							<Format>
								<MimeType>application/x-dfx</MimeType>
								<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
							</Format>
						</Default>
						<Supported>
							<Format>
								<MimeType>application/x-dfx</MimeType>
								<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
							</Format>
						</Supported>
					</ComplexData>
			</Input>	
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>TipusAtribut</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Type of Attribute</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract><![CDATA[<ul><li>1 Integer numbres ignoring texts and rounding if necessary.</li><li>2 Real numbers ignoring texts.</li><li> 3 3 Alphanumerical (texts and numbers) (not valid with altimetry entities filters).</li></ul>]]></ows:Abstract>
						<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param4" />
						<LiteralData>
						<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer "> integer</ows:DataType>
							<ows:Value>1</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>2</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>3</ows:Value>
						</ows:AllowedValues>
					</LiteralData>
			</Input>			
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Filtre</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Filter</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Objects filter:<![CDATA[<ul><li>
    1 Objects from all the layers</li><li>2 Objects from one layer</li><li>3 Objects from several layers from a file with one column equivalencies.</li><li>4 One text in any layer (only valid in options 3, 4 and 5).</li><li>5 Several texts in all the layers from a file of equivalences. (only valid in options 3, 4 and 5).</li><li>6 Altimetry: attribute will be deduced from the Z of the first vertex.</li><li>7 Altimetry from a file that contains the desired layers.</li><li>8 Block descripcions</li></ul>]]></ows:Abstract>
						<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param5" />
						<LiteralData>
						<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer "> integer</ows:DataType>
							<ows:Value>1</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>2</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>3</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>4</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>5</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>6</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>7</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>8</ows:Value>
						</ows:AllowedValues>
					</LiteralData>
			</Input>			
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>N_Decimals</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Number of Decimals</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the number of decimal figures written in the coordinates of the output file; its default value is 6.</ows:Abstract>
						<LiteralData>
						<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer "> integer</ows:DataType>
							<ows:Value>1</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>2</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>3</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>4</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>5</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>6</ows:Value>
						</ows:AllowedValues>
						<DefaultValue>6</DefaultValue>
					</LiteralData>
			</Input>	
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Tolerància</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Tolerance</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the maximum tolerated error when converting arcs, circles ellipses and curvatures between vertices DXF to VEC polylines. It can be used only with option 1. By default is 0.</ows:Abstract>
						<LiteralData>
						<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer "> integer</ows:DataType>
							<ows:AnyValue/>
						</ows:AllowedValues>
						<DefaultValue>0</DefaultValue>
					</LiteralData>
			</Input>			
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>3D</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>3D</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>1 means you want to import 3rt dimension from DXF file. 0 means you don't want to import. If the parameter isn't indicated, the program determines if DXF file si 2D o 3D file and choose the appropiated VEC format.</ows:Abstract>
						<LiteralData>
						<ows:AllowedValues>
	<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer "> integer</ows:DataType>
							<ows:Value>0</ows:Value>
							<ows:Value>1</ows:Value>	
						</ows:AllowedValues>
						<DefaultValue>0</DefaultValue>
					</LiteralData>
			</Input>			
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FITX_EQUIV</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Equivalences file</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the name of the equivalences file when using entities filters 3, 5 and 7. If it isn't indicated, the name will be asked during execution.</ows:Abstract>
						<ComplexData>
						<Default>
							<Format>
								<MimeType>application/x-txt</MimeType>
								<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
							</Format>
						</Default>
						<Supported>
							<Format>
								<MimeType>application/x-txt</MimeType>
								<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
							</Format>
						</Supported>
					</ComplexData>
			</Input>	
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>CAPA</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Capa</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the name of the layer to import using the filter 2. If it isn't indicated, the name will be asked during execution.</ows:Abstract>
						<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>ATRIBUT</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Atributte</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the atributte that substitutes the name of the layer to import using the filters 2 and 3. If it isn't indicated and you have indicated /CAPA, it takes the same valor; on the contrary, it will be asked during execution.</ows:Abstract>
						<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>			
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>TEXT</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Text</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the name of the text to import. If it isn't indicated, the name will be asked during execution.</ows:Abstract>
						<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>	
			</DataInputs>
		<ProcessOutputs>
			<Output>
				<ows:Identifier>F_VEC</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Vectorial file</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Usually it is the name of the output VEC file. It is the extraction directory when using the filter 8.
				</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param3" />
						<ComplexOutput>
							<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-VEC</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-VEC</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
						</ComplexOutput>
			</Output>
		</ProcessOutputs>
	</ProcessDescription>
